# Library

A small shelf of six books, each a card with a `genre` and a page count:
[[dune]], [[frankenstein]] and [[the-hobbit]] are novels;
[[a-room-of-ones-own]] and [[the-common-reader]] are essays; [[leaves-of-grass]]
is poetry. Three genres of three, two and one books, so a count per genre is
never a tie.

The shelf exists to be grouped and reduced. A query over it is a pipeline of
stages — filter, map, group, reduce — and the vault is small enough that every
result can be checked by hand, which is what makes it a fair oracle for any
execution backend.

The novels, computed from the cards:

```hql#eval
cards
| filter(c => c.metadata.genre == "novel")
| sort(by = c => c.name)
| map(c => c.title)
```
